  "description": "CR 702.103g a bestowed Aura that phases in unattached is a creature again (control: its host stays, so it phases in still attached and still bestowed)",
  "note": "The only road to 'phases in unattached' is a direct phase-out (CR 702.26i) whose host leaves meanwhile: an Aura dragged indirectly comes back attached whatever happened. Clever Concealment names the bestowed Rollicker alone, and Doom Blade kills the Piker while it is away. The card types and P/T are read, not just the attachment, since an Aura that merely came back detached is still an Enchantment with no P/T. The control is the same board with the host left alive: the Rollicker comes back an Aura still on the Piker, separating 'phasing in unbestowed it' from 'it was never bestowed'.",
